---
import PageIntro from "@/components/PageIntro.astro";
import SiteFooter from "@/components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "@/components/SiteHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={`Privacy policy for ${siteConfig.name}.`}>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="content">
    <div class="reading">
      <PageIntro
        title="Privacy"
        description="No ads. No selling your data. Here’s what happens when you use the site."
      />
    </div>

    <section class="reading section--tight">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="t-small t-dim">Last updated: 30 September 2026</p>

        <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
        <p>
          {siteConfig.name} is operated by <strong>OPERATOR NAME</strong>, responsible for
          the personal data handled through this site. Address: <strong>OPERATOR ADDRESS</strong>.
          For privacy questions or requests, contact <strong>PRIVACY EMAIL</strong>.
        </p>

        <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare Pages hosts and delivers the site. When you visit, Cloudflare processes
          technical information such as your IP address, requested URL, browser information,
          and request time to deliver pages and protect against abuse. Its security features
          may use cookies, depending on the protection applied. See
          the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>
          and <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/">cookie information</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Preferences and search</h2>
        <p>
          Your light or dark theme choice is saved in your browser under <code>mailer-theme</code>.
          It stays there until you change it or clear the site’s browser data. We don’t use it to
          track you. Search matches articles in your browser; we don’t maintain a separate search-history database.
          Search terms included in a page URL can still appear in hosting request logs.
        </p>

        <h2>Comments</h2>
        <p>
          Issue pages load Giscus, which displays comments from GitHub Discussions. Your browser
          connects to these services when comments load, even if you don’t post. To comment,
          you sign in with GitHub. Your comment, GitHub username, and profile picture are public.
          Don’t post anything you want kept private.
        </p>
        <p>
          Giscus stores an encrypted sign-in token in your browser when you sign in.
          Comments remain on GitHub until removed; you can manage your own comments there.
          See the <a href="https://github.com/giscus/giscus/blob/main/PRIVACY-POLICY.md">Giscus privacy policy</a>
          and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Emotes and outside links</h2>
        <p>
          Emotes load from 7TV and BetterTTV. Loading one sends its provider your IP address
          and browser request information, and may send referrer information. Their policies:
          <a href="https://7tv.app/legal/privacy">7TV</a> and
          <a href="https://betterttv.com/privacy">BetterTTV</a>.
          Following an outside link or using a social sharing link takes you to a service with
          its own privacy rules.
        </p>

        <h2>Email and the newsletter</h2>
        <p>
          If you email us, we use your address and message to reply and handle your request.
          We keep correspondence only as long as needed for that purpose or any legal obligation.
          Email provider: <strong>EMAIL PROVIDER</strong>.
          Newsletter signup is currently inactive and does not submit email addresses.
          We’ll update this policy with the provider, consent, and unsubscribe details before enabling it.
        </p>

        <h2>Ads and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We don’t run ads or sell personal data. The site’s code has no advertising trackers
          or analytics scripts configured.
          <strong> ANALYTICS SETUP: confirm whether Cloudflare Web Analytics or other dashboard-injected tracking is enabled, then replace this note with its details.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2>Why we process data</h2>
        <p>
          Where EU or UK data protection law applies, we rely on legitimate interests to deliver
          and secure the site, display its content and discussions, and answer messages
          (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)). We use consent where required for optional tracking or subscriptions
          (Article 6(1)(a)), and legal obligation where we must retain information by law
          (Article 6(1)(c)). Reading the site does not count as consent to optional tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>Storage and your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Providers may process data outside your country, including in the United States.
          Their linked policies explain retention and international-transfer safeguards.
          We don’t set their independent retention periods.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on applicable law, you can request access, correction, deletion, restriction,
          or a portable copy of your data, and object to processing based on legitimate interests.
          You can withdraw consent at any time without affecting earlier lawful processing.
          Contact <strong>PRIVACY EMAIL</strong> to make a request. You can also complain to your
          local data protection authority. For data held independently by GitHub or another provider,
          you may need to contact them directly.
        </p>
        <p>
          We’ll update this page when our setup changes and show the latest revision date above.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
